{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Plan-review advisory accepted (verified against scripts/mutation_sandbox.py _sb_quote): test_profile_denies_writes_then_permits_the_allow_list never runs sandbox-exec; it fails on Windows because the profile escapes each backslash of the path while the test expects the raw path. It is fixed by comparing with the escaped form, not skipped. Only test_profile_escapes_quotes_and_backslashes_in_paths stays intentionally unsupported (a directory name containing a double quote is invalid on Windows, WinError 123). Evidence for the on-main ACs comes from the scheduled main sweep after merge; the tmp/w3-owl run is the pre-push check."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1795258793268590001,"uuid":"6313f152-9fcf-4dc4-ace1-eb17a96b9464"}